{% extends 'demos/pagination/demo.html.twig' %}

{% block demo_container %}
    <div class="LivePaginationStage max-w-[1220px] mx-auto mb-12">
        <twig:Browser
            class="LivePaginationBrowser shadow-blur shadow-blur--rainbow w-full"
            frameClass="aspect-[3/2]"
        >
            <twig:LivePagination paginationRoute="app_demo_pagination_live" />
        </twig:Browser>
    </div>

    <section class="LivePaginationExplanation py-12" style="padding-top: 6rem;">
        <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-6 md:px-12">
            <twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow
                filename="src/Twig/Components/LivePagination.php"
                :lineStart="30"
                :lineEnd="52"
            >
## A filterable catalog

`color` and `pattern` are URL-bound LiveProps. The component receives its
repository through ordinary Symfony dependency injection.

`createPagination()` starts from the filtered repository query, preserves the
active filters in generated URLs, and asks for 10 jerseys at a time.
            </twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="LivePaginationExplanation py-12">
        <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-6 md:px-12">
            <twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow
                filename="src/Twig/Components/LivePagination.php"
                :lineStart="20"
                :lineEnd="28"
                reversed
                sticky
            >
## Add the pagination trait

`ComponentWithPaginationTrait` adds the writable page state and the actions
that move forward, backward, or to a specific page.

The component does not need to implement that state or duplicate the navigation
logic itself.
            </twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="LivePaginationExplanation py-12">
        <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-6 md:px-12">
            <twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow
                filename="src/Twig/Components/LivePagination.php"
                :lineStart="68"
                :lineEnd="95"
                sticky
            >
## Reset after a filter changes

`toggleFilter()` validates the selected option and updates the corresponding
LiveProp before the component renders the filtered query again.

`resetPage()` returns to page 1 first. A smaller filtered result can never leave
the component stranded on a page that no longer exists.
            </twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="LivePaginationExplanation py-12">
        <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto px-6 md:px-12">
            <twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow
                filename="templates/components/LivePagination/Pagination.html.twig"
                reversed
                sticky
            >
## Enhance ordinary links

`ux_pagination()` still renders real links. `paginationLinkAttributes` adds the
Live action that updates only this component when JavaScript is available.

The same markup keeps its normal navigation fallback, and the selected theme
does not need any LiveComponent-specific code.
            </twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow>
        </div>
    </section>
{% endblock %}
